  "model_final_text": "I inspected the actual controller, robot model, and all three authoritative scenarios, then ran and verified simulations.\n\n### Cause\nThe collision is caused by the controller\u2019s fixed braking trigger:\n\n- `robot/controller.py` brakes only when `wall_clearance <= 0.12 m`\n- It ignores:\n  - robot mass\n  - current speed\n  - actuator braking authority\n  - required safety clearance\n  - discrete-time reaction effects\n\n### Evidence\nBaseline controller failed in all scenarios:\n\n- **A**: brakes at `0.12 m`, but physics predicts it needs about **0.36 m** to stop from `1.2 m/s` with `2.0 kg` and `4 N` braking.  \n  Result: wall contact at `0.97 m/s`.\n- **B**: heavier robot (`3.0 kg`) needs about **0.54 m** to stop.  \n  Result: wall contact at `1.05 m/s`.\n- **C**: changed wall location and initial speed; still needs about **0.25 m** to stop.  \n  Result: wall contact at `0.71 m/s`.\n\nThose are measured simulation results, independently verified.\n\n### Repair proposed\nI submitted a controller-only patch that:\n\n- computes braking onset from **measured stopping distance**\n- uses actual:\n  - carriage mass\n  - actuator force limits\n  - timestep\n  - current velocity\n- includes a **reaction buffer**\n- keeps braking latched near the wall so it doesn\u2019t release too early\n- actively damps residual reverse motion so final speed settles below the limit\n\n### Verification result\nThe second proposal was independently executed and **passed A/B/C**:\n\n- **Candidate:** `candidate_9ba053aaee684edf8f1914731a5449fc`\n\nMeasured outcomes:\n\n- **A**: min clearance `0.0524 m`, final speed ~`0`\n- **B**: min clearance `0.05237 m`, final speed ~`0`\n- **C**: min clearance `0.05255 m`, final speed ~`0`\n\nAll passed:\n- zero wall contact events\n- minimum clearance \u2265 `0.05 m`\n- final speed < `0.03 m/s`\n\n### Concise diagnosis\nThe wall collision was not a MuJoCo or geometry issue; it was a controller design defect. A fixed `0.12 m` trigger is too late and does not generalize across masses or environments. A stopping-distance-based controller fixes that and was independently verified across the provided robot/world variants.",
